Local review patch: require consistent T6032 TZ maps across all planes
Base: m1n1 4184923ffb2dff079b384d6a32cc02142aa14572, after 0001..0012
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Do not assume controller 0, plane 0 represents all sixteen controllers and
four planes. Validate descriptors before reading, then compare each slot's
enable state and, when enabled, its start/end words across all contexts.
Disabled slots' unused limit words may differ. Preserve the existing
nonzero-enable interpretation and staged mapping/heap/publication effects.
Reject differences rather than unioning ranges into the four-slot model.

This raises the worst-case read count from 12 to 768. It is not an atomic
snapshot, an access-permission check, or a bound on a stalled MMIO read.
Early-access/recovery qualification and explicit native authorization are
still required. No firmware is executed by preparing/testing this patch.

--- a/src/mcc.c
+++ b/src/mcc.c
@@ -443,12 +443,31 @@
         return -1;
+    /* Check every descriptor before the first register access. */
+    for (int controller = 0; controller < T6032_MCC_INSTANCE_COUNT; controller++) {
+        if (mcc_regs[controller].tz != &t6031_tz_regs ||
+            mcc_regs[controller].plane_count != 4 ||
+            mcc_regs[controller].plane_stride != T6031_PLANE_STRIDE)
+            return -1;
+    }
     u64 heap_limit = old_limit && old_limit < ram_end ? old_limit : ram_end;
 
-    /* Same controller/plane/slots as the legacy path; this does not prove their layout. */
+    /* Require a common sampled map; this does not establish access safety or stability. */
     for (u32 i = 0; i < PLANE_TZ_MAX_REGS; i++) {
         u64 off = (u64)t6031_tz_regs.stride * i;
         u32 first = plane_read32(0, 0, t6031_tz_regs.start + off);
         u32 last = plane_read32(0, 0, t6031_tz_regs.end + off);
         bool enabled = plane_read32(0, 0, t6031_tz_regs.enable + off);
+        for (int controller = 0; controller < T6032_MCC_INSTANCE_COUNT; controller++) {
+            for (int plane = 0; plane < 4; plane++) {
+                if (!controller && !plane)
+                    continue;
+                u32 other_first = plane_read32(controller, plane, t6031_tz_regs.start + off);
+                u32 other_last = plane_read32(controller, plane, t6031_tz_regs.end + off);
+                bool other_enabled = plane_read32(controller, plane, t6031_tz_regs.enable + off);
+                if (other_enabled != enabled ||
+                    (enabled && (other_first != first || other_last != last)))
+                    return -1;
+            }
+        }
         if (!enabled)
             continue;
         struct mcc_carveout candidate;
